<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tawergha</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tawargha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tawergha is a town in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>, south of Misrata, on the route along the coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-sirte">Gulf of Sirte</a>. In 761 an Abbasid army defeated and killed the Ibadi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> Abu al-Khattab nearby. In 2011, during the Libyan civil war, its population was expelled by Misratan militias.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tawergha.jpg" alt="Tawergha" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bashirforlibya · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%B9%D9%8A%D9%86_%D8%AA%D8%A7%D9%88%D8%B1%D8%BA%D8%A7%D8%A1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
